<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH JIHOMORAVSKA 1996 NET PROFIT FALLS.</title>
<headline>CZECH JIHOMORAVSKA 1996 NET PROFIT FALLS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech power utility Jihomoravska Energetika a.s. said on Wednesday its audited net profit fell to 425 million crowns last year from 510 million in</p>
<p>1995, according to Czech accounting standards.</p>
<p>Results for year ending December 31, 1996 (in millions of</p>
<p>crowns):</p>
<p> Net profit		  424.60    vs	  510.28</p>
<p> Gross profit		564.96    vs	  806.75</p>
<p> Operating profit	  618.81    vs	  833.19</p>
<p>Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services	   11,869.82    vs     11,174.86</p>
<p> Total assets	   11,121.03    vs	9,271.39</p>
<p> Basic capital	   3,531.57    vs	3,484.28</p>
<p>NOTE: The company is a regional power distributor, based in</p>
<p>the Czech city of Brno. The board plans to propose to</p>
<p>shareholders a 51 crown gross dividend payout on 1996 earnings,</p>
<p>after a 40 crown dividend last year.</p>
<p>Jihomoraska shares are listed on the main market of the</p>
<p>Prague Stock Exchange. Jihomoravska is one of the country's</p>
<p>eight regional electricity companies, which should be further</p>
<p>privatised under a government plan to speed up the sale of</p>
<p>strategic assets.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
